### Custom node with Handle connection points

Source: https://reactflow.dev/llms-full.txt

Use this custom node component to define connection points with the Handle component. It renders a target handle on the left and a source handle on the right. The props type is exported as HandleProps for TypeScript users.

```jsx
import { Handle, Position } from '@xyflow/react';

export const CustomNode = ({ data }) => {
  return (
    <>
      <div style={{ padding: '10px 20px' }}>
        {data.label}
      </div>

      <Handle type="target" position={Position.Left} />
      <Handle type="source" position={Position.Right} />
    </>
  );
};
```

